verse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "db5e1eaa-c7d3-5b24-b145-019eca21ce7f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423273}}] :activity/title "Matrices With Easy-to-Find Inverses" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423257}]}
